Why is a no-arg constructor needed in JPA?
    JPA (Java Persistence API) requires that every entity class has a public or protected no-argument constructor, for the following reasons:
    When JPA (via Hibernate or any ORM) creates objects while reading from the database, it uses reflection.
    It does not use your custom constructors — instead, it:
    Instantiates the entity using the no-arg constructor Then sets fields one-by-one using reflection

