🔄 What is a Circular Reference in Java/Spring Boot?
A circular reference happens when two objects reference each other in a loop — this becomes problematic especially during JSON serialization.

@Entity
public class Post {
    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "post", cascade = CascadeType.ALL)
    private List<Comment> comments;
}

@Entity
public class Comment {
    @ManyToOne
    @JoinColumn(name = "post_id")
    private Post post;
}

🔁 When Returned as JSON:
When you return a Post, it contains comments, and each Comment contains the post again, and again...
Post {
  comments: [
    { post: { comments: [...] } }
  ]
}
This leads to:
❌ StackOverflowError
❌ "Infinite recursion" error in Postman / console logs


